# Deploy the springblades in the MIDDLE of a fight, then strike.
#
# This is the measured half of bd inc-tek.8.8, finding PA-08-F14. The free
# off-guard strike is meant to be worth one opening; it must not be available
# to a wielder who is already engaged.
#
# HOW THE RUN GETS "ALREADY ENGAGED", and why it is the engine's own state and
# not the script's opinion. Creature::isFlatFooted() is a per-creature
# out-of-combat counter, FFCount > min(5,10+Mod(A_WIS)) (inc/Creature.h:571-572).
# Any strike zeroes it for both fighters (src/Fight.cpp:3258-3259) and
# Creature::DoTurn() raises it by one per turn out of combat
# (src/Creature.cpp:1590-1591). So the run kills the first goblin with the
# character's ordinary knife, which zeroes the counter, and only then snaps the
# blades out.
#
# THE STATE IS VISIBLE. The sidebar prints "Exploring" when isFlatFooted() is
# true and "Fighting" when it is false (src/Term.cpp:388-392). Every dump here
# carries it, and tools/check_springblade.sh reads the word off the dump where
# the blades snapped out rather than assuming what the run arranged.
#
# THE SECOND GOBLIN is summoned after the first is dead, so the strike that is
# measured lands on a fresh creature. That matters: it means the only
# difference between this run and springblade-cold.keys is the wielder's own
# counter, which is the one thing the fix reads.
#
# EIGHT ACTIVATION ATTEMPTS. A rogue fails the DC 15 Handle Device check the
# fix adds more often than not. A jammed attempt costs a round and nothing
# else. Jams do carry the wielder back towards "Exploring" -- one FFCount per
# turn -- which is why the check reads the sidebar instead of trusting the
# arrangement.

@include springblade-setup.keys

# ------------------------------------------------------- the fight starts
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:0001-first-goblin

RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:0002-knife-strike

# ------------------------------------------------------- a fresh victim
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
LEFT ENTER
@dump:0003-second-goblin

# ------------------------------------------------------- deploy, engaged
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0004-deploy-1
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0005-deploy-2
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0006-deploy-3
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0007-deploy-4
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0008-deploy-5
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0009-deploy-6
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0010-deploy-7
a
@choose "Springblade Bracers"
@dump:0011-deploy-8

LEFT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@dump:0012-strike

@quit
